intent: >
  Add a homepage section that promotes Tustin, Orange, and Villa Park as
  Steve's primary service areas without removing the broader coverage
  list, so the marketing emphasis shifts toward the three focus areas
  while honest 'we serve all of OC' messaging stays intact.

slice: "?/?"
kind: feature
behavior_change: additive

reversibility: trivial

scope:
  declared:
    - src/index.njk
  actual:
    - src/index.njk
  drift: []

proof:
  tests_run: "Manual: dev server + Chrome via mcp__claude-in-chrome. Verified section ID 'primary-areas' present, section appears between 'working-with-steve' and 'services' in section order, all three city cards render with correct headings (Tustin & North Tustin, Orange, Villa Park) and correct service-area page hrefs (/service-areas/tustin/, /service-areas/orange/, /service-areas/villa-park/), TODO Steve markers stripped from served HTML, zero new em-dashes introduced."
  result: green
  failing: 0

tests:
  needed: "no"
  rationale: >
    Static Nunjucks template, no logic. Verified by DOM inspection.

assumptions:
  - "navigation.json already orders serviceAreas with Tustin/Orange/Villa Park first. Verified — the existing footer iteration already produces them in the right order, no JSON change needed."
  - "The existing 'Some of the Areas We Serve' grid in the About section stays intact and lists all 11 areas. Visitors who care about whether Steve serves a specific area can find it there."
  - "Steve will rewrite the one-sentence city descriptions to match how he actually thinks about each area. The placeholder copy is best-guess (estate gardens in Tustin, Old Towne in Orange, larger estates in Villa Park)."
  - "Lime border-left treatment is enough visual distinction without screaming 'these are different'. The cards still match the rest of the page's component vocabulary, just with one extra cue."

specifications:
  - "Primary Service Areas live in a single section between Working with Steve and Services, with section ID 'primary-areas'."
  - "Section refuses to know about services or about Steve's bio. Those belong in adjacent sections."
  - "Section refuses to claim Steve doesn't serve other areas. Intro paragraph explicitly says 'He works across Orange County, but these three are home.'"
  - "Each card is wholly clickable (whole <a>) AND has a visible CTA line at the bottom for older / less tech-savvy visitors to recognize it as a link. Same pattern as the accessibility PR's service grid update."
  - "Card visual treatment: bg-gray-50 (vs. white section bg), border-l-4 border-lime, shadow on hover. Distinguishable from the generic Services cards on the same page."

deviations_from_plan: >
  Plan said 'reorder navigation.json serviceAreas to put Tustin/Orange/
  Villa Park first.' Turned out they were already first in the array. No
  reorder needed; nav.json untouched. Surfacing because the plan listed
  it as a step.

  Plan said 'add homepage Primary Service Areas block.' Did that.

  No deviation on intent or scope; the JSON step was just a confirmed
  no-op.

trade_offs: >
  Chose NOT to restructure the existing About section to move the 11-city
  grid OUT of it and into a separate 'Additional Service Areas' section
  below the new Primary block. That would have given a cleaner top-to-
  bottom hierarchy (focus first, full coverage second) but required
  splitting About's 2-column layout, which is more disruptive than the
  user asked for. The current order (full list inside About, focus block
  after Working with Steve) is honest and works as a hierarchy.

  Chose NOT to remove the 8 non-focus areas from the footer. The footer
  iterates navigation.json's serviceAreas; removing them there would have
  hidden them across every page, which conflicts with 'Steve still
  serves these areas'.

  Chose 'Where Steve Focuses' as the section eyebrow rather than
  'Primary Service Areas' as the H2. Concierge voice — Steve is the
  subject, not the abstract noun.

interfaces:
  consumed:
    - "/service-areas/tustin/ (existing) — card link target"
    - "/service-areas/orange/ (existing) — card link target"
    - "/service-areas/villa-park/ (existing) — card link target"

self_review:
  consistency: >
    Card markup follows the established Lytle pattern: <a> wraps the card,
    group classes for hover propagation, icon + heading + p + CTA pattern.
    The lime border-l-4 is a new visual element but uses the existing
    lime brand color.
  metz: N/A — Nunjucks template.
  body_plan: >
    New section has one job: visually promote Tustin/Orange/Villa Park.
    Refuses to do anything else. Drawable: positioned between 'how Steve
    works' and 'what Steve does', completing the homeowner journey:
    impression -> person -> method -> location -> offerings -> proof ->
    CTA.
  honesty: >
    Section explicitly says 'He works across Orange County, but these
    three are home.' That's the actual situation Steve described.
    Doesn't claim exclusivity; doesn't hide the broader coverage.

confidence: high
reviewer_attention:
  - "src/index.njk:196-198  — section intro paragraph. The 'He works across Orange County, but these three are home' line is the body-plan refusal stated out loud. Worth a sanity check that it reads honestly to Steve."
  - "src/index.njk:202-206, 209-213, 216-220  — three card descriptions. Best-guess characterizations of each area's distinctive work. Steve should overwrite with his actual sense of each market."
